# Pairs with SetSagaConsistent. The capture that skips the drain gate - and,
# because the gate's re-check would otherwise refuse the attempt, the
# re-check too. A cross-tree saga registered before the fence finalizes on
# one tree before its gate and not on the other, which then resolves it
# against a snapshot with no local decision, pre-saga, beside the first
# tree's post-saga terminal. Its registration predates the drain, so the
# epoch validation cannot see it.
MODULE: SetSagaConsistentSkipsDrainAndRecheck
TARGET: SetSagaConsistent
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the drain gate passes with delegation rows live, and the gated re-check is skipped
PERTURBS: DrainGate, Recheck

--- FIND
    /\ phase = "drain"
    /\ \A T \in Members : ~InFlight(T)
--- REPLACE
    /\ phase = "drain"
    \* MUTATION: no wait for the rows to drain.
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ IF kind = "single" \/ \A T \in Members : ~InFlight(T)
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: no re-check.
    /\ IF TRUE
--- END
